Source: Assessment and Assessment Flexibility Policy
Section: Section 3 - Policy > Responsibilities in Assessment

(27) Deans/Heads of School/Cluster Directors are responsible for:
1. applying university assessment policy and processes in their school, industry cluster or centre;
2. convening course assessment committees and program assessment boards for each program in accordance with the membership and terms of reference in the relevant section of the assessment processes;
3. submission of results for courses in accordance with the schedule set by the University Secretary and Academic Registrar;
4. in higher education courses, ensuring that moderation processes are conducted systematically in accordance with the course assessment committees, program assessment boards and moderation sections of the Assessment Processes
5. ensuring that validation of assessment in vocational education is undertaken in accordance with the validation of assessment: Vocational Education section of the assessment processes.
6. These responsibilities apply irrespective of delivery mode and location.

Source: Assessment and Assessment Flexibility Policy
Section: Section 3 - Policy > Academic Progress

(67) Chairs of program assessment boards are responsible for:
1. reviewing the progress of students in accordance with the academic progress (coursework programs) section of the assessment processes;
2. determining the stage of unsatisfactory progress of students: First stage – at risk of unsatisfactory academic progress Final stage – established unacceptable academic progress in more than one teaching period;
3. ensuring that where a student is identified as at risk of unsatisfactory academic progress there is an intervention to offer the student academic advice and support to improve their performance.
